# uv replaces pip, venv, pyenv and pipx with one binary. The rows below are the
# handful you use daily; `uv --help` lists 24 subcommands and each of those has
# its own — `uv tool install` alone has 63 flags, which is exactly why they are
# fetched on demand and not written out here.
name:    uv
what:    Python packaging — venvs, installs, tools, and Python itself
check:   uv
install: curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh \| sh
docs:    uv help <command>, docs.astral.sh/uv
probe:   help

= A PROJECT
uv init NAME     | new project with a pyproject.toml
uv add PKG       | add a dependency, resolve, and install it
uv add --dev PKG | a dev-only dependency
uv remove PKG    | drop one
uv sync          | make the venv match the lockfile. The one to run after a pull
uv lock          | re-resolve and rewrite uv.lock
uv tree          | the dependency tree, with who pulled what in

= RUNNING THINGS
@uv run          | run a command inside the project venv, syncing first
  --no-sync      | skip the sync when you know it is current
  --with PKG     | add a package for this run only
uv run script.py | no activate step, ever
uv run pytest    | the same for any installed tool

= TOOLS — the pipx replacement
uv tool install NAME | install a CLI into its own isolated venv
uv tool list     | what you have installed this way
uv tool upgrade --all | upgrade all of them
uv tool uninstall NAME | remove one
uvx NAME         | run a tool WITHOUT installing it. Short for `uv tool run`

= PYTHON ITSELF
uv python list   | which interpreters uv can see, installed or downloadable
uv python install 3.12 | fetch one
uv venv          | make a .venv here
uv venv --python 3.12 | ... with a specific interpreter

= THE pip COMPATIBILITY LAYER
uv pip install PKG | same arguments as pip, much faster
uv pip list      | what is in the active environment
uv pip freeze    | the same, as requirements lines
uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt | the pip-tools replacement
uv pip sync requirements.txt | make the env match that file exactly

= HOUSEKEEPING
uv cache dir     | where the cache lives
uv cache clean   | empty it
uv self update   | update uv itself

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
